  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="req-h">
    <h2 id="req-h">Requirements</h2>
    <p><strong>Bahr Family Properties Leasing Procedure for Rental Homes</strong></p>

    <h3>To Apply to Rent this Home:</h3>
    <ul class="plain-list">
      <li>Go to this website to complete our free screening: <a href="https://bfpapply.lovable.app">bfpapply.lovable.app</a>. You will upload IDs for all adults, paycheck stubs, and your housing voucher if applicable as part of the application. Screening takes roughly 2 business days.</li>
      <li>If you pass our minimum screening criteria, we will schedule a time to view the home.</li>
      <li>After your showing, if you decide you want to move forward, we will run a credit and background check. The fee for the check is $32.
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li>Note: Every occupant over 18 will need to be included, and the $32 fee applies to each adult.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>As a final step, we will go over our standard lease with you.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>AS A REMINDER, our screening criteria is:</p>
    <ul class="plain-list">
      <li>If you have a Section 8 voucher: monthly income of at least 1.5 times the rent
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li>If you do not have a voucher, monthly income of at least 3 times the rent</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>Positive references from previous landlords, including no past due amounts owed, no damages and no significant lease violations.</li>
      <li>No prior evictions (within 5 years).</li>
      <li>No bad criminal history.</li>
      <li>No smoking inside the home, of any substance including marijuana.</li>
      <li>No outstanding collections to utility companies.</li>
      <li>Mostly positive pay history on credit report for last 1 to 2 years. We have no minimum credit score; however, scores under 550 require a double deposit of two months rent.</li>
      <li>Animals are allowed on a case by case basis, with a $250 animal deposit and $25/month animal rent.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>To Lease the Home:</h3>
    <ul class="plain-list">
      <li>Meet with property manager to review the lease and/or complete Housing Authority paperwork.
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li>You will need to provide half of the deposit at this time. (If you have a voucher, your deposit is a flat $1,000, so half is $500.) The other half is due on or before the move in date and before you can occupy the property.</li>
          <li>The 50% is refundable if you are unable to occupy property due to circumstances outside of your control (landlord cancels, Housing Authority cancels, Landlord and Housing Authority are unable to come to an agreement on rent, condition, etc. in a timely manner).</li>
          <li>The 50% is non-refundable if you cancel occupancy for a reason not listed above.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>To Move In/Get Keys for the Home:</h3>
    <p>On or about the lease start date, meet with the property manager to do a walk through of the home and obtain keys. In order to get the keys to the home you will need to bring:</p>
    <ul class="plain-list">
      <li>Remaining security deposit, first month’s rent and landlord-billed utilities (such as sewer &amp; trash — varies by home) - If you do not have a housing voucher and your credit score is below 550, the double deposit described above applies.
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li>Note: Tenants receiving Section 8 assistance will only be responsible for their portion of their first month’s rent and landlord-billed utilities</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>Occupancy Permit from local municipality (if applicable)</li>
      <li>Proof that utilities have been transferred into your name</li>
      <li>Proof of renter’s insurance.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="s8-h">
    <h2 id="s8-h">Section 8 welcome</h2>
    <p>Housing Choice Vouchers (Section 8) are welcome at Bahr Family Properties. All our homes accept vouchers, and voucher holders apply the same way as everyone else — same application, same screening.</p>
  </section>
